		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">46</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of the array in paper.
2. Now I will start from first element of the array and change each element to its square 
3. Now I will apply it to all other elements of the array
4. Now I will sort the array.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">126.67100297790412</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3535.558052308455</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">466.6825497509953</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">254.482998015921</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of the array in paper.
2. Now I will start from first element of the array and change each element to its square 
3. Now I will apply it to all other elements of the array
4. Now I will sort the array.</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">466.6825497509953</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">111.65625</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">47</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.

We have 3 major phases in the implementation.
Phase 1: One is to read the elements of the array.
Phase 2: Second is squaring the elements of the array
Phase 3: Third is sorting the array

Phase 1
1. Read the length of the array
2. Create an empty array.
3. Read the next value from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all the elements of the array.
Phase 2
6. Now go to index 0 element of the array.
7. Replace the that element with the square of that element.
8. Now move to next element
9. Repeat steps 12,13 untill we reach the end of array.
Phase 3
10. Now sort the array in ascending order.
11. Now start displaying elements of array from index 0 to last element in separate lines.
</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">-17.96125159311697</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3893.796938255102</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">784.5999100020969</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">344.5924301273707</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I came up with.

We have 3 major phases in the implementation.
Phase 1: One is to read the elements of the array.
Phase 2: Second is squaring the elements of the array
Phase 3: Third is sorting the array

Phase 1
1. Read the length of the array
2. Create an empty array.
3. Read the next value from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all the elements of the array.
Phase 2
6. Now go to index 0 element of the array.
7. Replace the that element with the square of that element.
8. Now move to next element
9. Repeat steps 12,13 untill we reach the end of array.
Phase 3
10. Now sort the array in ascending order.
11. Now start displaying elements of array from index 0 to last element in separate lines.
</attribute>
